WEBVTT

00:06.297 --> 00:08.258
I'm pooped, woman.

00:10.176 --> 00:15.306
<i>Hit me once every ten seconds</i>
<i>or I kill the boy.</i>

00:15.390 --> 00:18.768
<i>Honestly, I thought I was done for</i>
<i>when she said that,</i>

00:18.852 --> 00:20.270
<i>but Lu's doing pretty good.</i>

00:22.063 --> 00:23.356
Aw, no.

00:25.275 --> 00:27.610
Oh, lucky me.

00:27.694 --> 00:29.988
But I'm begging you,
please take the fight more seriously!

00:32.365 --> 00:33.658
My turn!

00:34.909 --> 00:36.202
Lu!

00:38.246 --> 00:39.789
Guess the fun's over.

00:39.873 --> 00:41.374
But you're better than I--

00:42.917 --> 00:43.752
No way.

00:46.379 --> 00:49.174
Shin, your voice cracked
when you said "Lu"!

00:51.843 --> 00:54.054
<i>Is she a happy drunk after all?</i>

01:03.313 --> 01:04.522
Oh, no.

01:11.863 --> 01:12.864
<i>Marvelous…</i>

01:14.449 --> 01:17.660
Give me more. Try to kill me.

01:17.744 --> 01:18.870
Huh?

01:18.953 --> 01:21.664
I don't kill, lady.

01:21.748 --> 01:25.126
It's against our family rule.

01:26.002 --> 01:26.836
Lu…

01:26.920 --> 01:30.048
Family rule? What are you talking about?

01:30.131 --> 01:33.635
Promises we keep as a family!

01:33.718 --> 01:36.888
Shin, Mr. Manager, Ms. Aoi, Hana,

01:36.971 --> 01:40.558
they're all my precious family!

01:41.017 --> 01:42.101
Huh?

01:42.185 --> 01:45.188
The Sakamotos are a family of three.

01:45.271 --> 01:46.231
Are you stupid?

01:46.898 --> 01:48.233
Stupid?

01:48.358 --> 01:52.153
I learned how to run a cash register
right after coming to Japan.

01:52.237 --> 01:56.324
Even Hana has her eye on me
for the next shift leader.

01:56.407 --> 01:57.742
And you have the nerve…

01:59.035 --> 02:01.788
to call me stupid, you bitch?

02:01.871 --> 02:03.498
<i>No, she's an angry drunk!</i>

02:04.207 --> 02:05.708
<i>Where's this power coming from?</i>

02:07.127 --> 02:08.378
Damn--

02:11.506 --> 02:12.340
What?

02:15.093 --> 02:15.927
What?

02:16.010 --> 02:17.554
What was I doing?

02:18.805 --> 02:20.306
Who's this lady?

02:21.057 --> 02:22.809
Oh, Shin.

02:22.892 --> 02:24.227
Whatcha doing?

02:24.310 --> 02:25.728
Where are we?

02:25.812 --> 02:28.565
<i>She sobered up all of a sudden!</i>

02:28.648 --> 02:33.153
Are you trying to let me off easy?
You've got some nerve!

02:34.654 --> 02:37.365
I can't remember the last time anyone's…

02:37.448 --> 02:38.283
<i>Shit!</i>

02:38.366 --> 02:40.493
…pushed me this far.

02:42.036 --> 02:44.706
I absolutely love strong rivals!

02:44.789 --> 02:48.001
You really gave me chills!

02:48.543 --> 02:51.796
-Come on, let's do one more round! Please?
-Are we… off the hook?

02:51.880 --> 02:52.964
Hey, stop it!

04:23.972 --> 04:25.974
10g of potassium perchlorate.

04:26.057 --> 04:27.558
SOURCE OF STRENGTH

04:27.642 --> 04:29.686
4.8g of ammonium nitrate.

04:30.603 --> 04:32.397
20g of P-thrite.

04:33.147 --> 04:35.358
3.5g of Nitro GK.

04:36.150 --> 04:38.152
I remember you now, Boiled.

04:40.697 --> 04:43.199
Time to show you what I can really do.

04:44.784 --> 04:46.536
I dunno what kind of trick that is,

04:46.619 --> 04:49.831
but what difference does it make
that you got a little thinner?

04:50.415 --> 04:53.334
If you want a fight,
you might wanna hurry.

04:53.418 --> 04:56.587
I bet your family's in a pinch too
right about now.

04:56.671 --> 04:58.548
I'm not worried about that.

04:58.631 --> 05:02.343
I have people that I can count on now.

05:03.678 --> 05:04.971
So what?

05:06.014 --> 05:06.889
<i>He's so fast…</i>

05:36.711 --> 05:40.173
<i>So this is the real Sakamoto,</i>
<i>the invincible hit man!</i>

05:47.597 --> 05:48.848
<i>But how?</i>

05:51.309 --> 05:56.606
<i>How can he still be so strong</i>
<i>after he quit being a hit man?</i>

05:59.275 --> 06:01.110
You're tough to beat, Boiled.

06:02.028 --> 06:06.282
Like you, I used to use my strength
to hurt people.

06:06.908 --> 06:08.910
But now…

06:10.995 --> 06:13.873
<i>I choose to use my strength</i>
<i>to protect the people I love.</i>

06:14.540 --> 06:15.750
That's…

06:17.376 --> 06:20.338
<i>what makes me strong now, Boiled.</i>

06:24.634 --> 06:27.095
Wow, this view is amazing!

06:27.178 --> 06:28.638
Yeah, it's beautiful.

06:29.263 --> 06:32.350
But not as beautiful as you…

06:33.184 --> 06:34.310
Satoshi?

06:36.437 --> 06:37.688
What was that?

06:43.653 --> 06:47.698
Sakamoto, I gotta give it to you…

06:47.782 --> 06:51.160
You're hard-boiled as hell.

06:59.502 --> 07:00.962
Hey, Shin?

07:03.589 --> 07:04.757
Ms. Aoi?

07:04.841 --> 07:07.135
I thought we were in the haunted house.

07:07.218 --> 07:08.427
How did we get here?

07:08.511 --> 07:11.639
We… must've all gotten worn out!

07:11.722 --> 07:13.391
It was pretty intense in there.

07:13.975 --> 07:16.144
How did your clothes get so dirty?

07:16.227 --> 07:19.605
Well, those zombies were tough, and--

07:19.689 --> 07:21.357
-Tough?
-Oops…

07:21.441 --> 07:22.567
Where's Taro?

07:22.650 --> 07:23.860
I dunno!

07:23.943 --> 07:25.570
I'll go look for him!

07:30.158 --> 07:32.702
Watch your step as you get off, please.

07:36.873 --> 07:39.250
Are you okay? What happened?

07:39.876 --> 07:41.919
-Little lady.
-Yes?

07:42.795 --> 07:44.964
Don't embarrass a guy…

07:46.132 --> 07:47.675
by asking him how he got hurt.

07:47.758 --> 07:50.136
No, I mean…
You're gonna have to pay for damages.

07:54.932 --> 07:56.767
You win, Sakamoto.

07:57.351 --> 07:59.145
I'll back off from you.

08:00.104 --> 08:01.981
But you're still gonna have…

08:04.901 --> 08:06.736
Five pork buns, coming right up!

08:07.737 --> 08:09.155
Not even listening, huh?

08:11.824 --> 08:13.493
That looks good.

08:13.576 --> 08:14.660
Can I have one?

08:20.041 --> 08:22.084
Your leftovers? How lucky of me.

08:23.794 --> 08:25.838
The rest is for my family.

08:25.922 --> 08:28.799
You, a family guy? Who would've thought.

08:28.883 --> 08:30.718
Mr. Sakamoto?!

08:33.429 --> 08:36.349
You're thin! Why? How?

08:36.432 --> 08:38.309
People lose weight when they work out.

08:38.392 --> 08:40.311
But not that much in a single day!

08:40.394 --> 08:43.689
You look just like you used to.
You're so cool!

08:43.773 --> 08:46.484
By the way, what are you gonna do
about that bounty?

08:46.567 --> 08:49.237
Dondenkai will keep trying to kill you.

08:49.320 --> 08:50.238
Well…

08:55.284 --> 08:57.495
Bounty?

08:57.578 --> 08:59.413
What's that about?

09:02.833 --> 09:04.710
<i>Why am I in trouble?</i>

09:06.128 --> 09:08.673
Hana, let's go over there and play.

09:08.756 --> 09:11.092
I want two cotton candies!

09:11.175 --> 09:12.927
What a self-indulgent child!

09:13.010 --> 09:14.262
Such potential for strength.

09:17.765 --> 09:18.683
So?

09:20.142 --> 09:22.311
There's a bounty on my head, and…

09:22.395 --> 09:24.730
hit men have been out to get me.

09:25.523 --> 09:26.691
Like today…

09:26.774 --> 09:29.527
Why on earth would you not tell me
something like that?!

09:31.279 --> 09:33.573
Men are clumsy creatures, miss.

09:34.031 --> 09:36.951
He just wanted you and your kid…

09:38.494 --> 09:43.040
to enjoy the amusement park
without worrying about anything.

09:44.750 --> 09:46.669
That's pretty hard-boiled, I'd say.

09:46.752 --> 09:48.671
And who are you?

09:48.754 --> 09:50.423
The name's Boiled.

09:50.965 --> 09:52.216
I'm a professional hit man.

09:52.300 --> 09:56.220
Would you mind not killing my husband?

09:56.846 --> 09:57.847
Yes, ma'am…

09:57.930 --> 10:00.558
Besides, did you really think
you could hide this?

10:01.142 --> 10:04.103
Well, I just… I didn't want to worry you.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.856
Have you forgotten?

10:07.398 --> 10:11.902
Sakamoto family rule number six.
"Do not hide things from each other"!

10:12.653 --> 10:16.407
I'd rather you go and put it all to rest
than go behind my back!

10:20.494 --> 10:23.205
Now that that's settled,

10:23.289 --> 10:25.124
let's go watch the parade.

10:27.835 --> 10:30.463
That's one hard-boiled wife you've got…

10:43.559 --> 10:47.897
But Mr. Sakamoto, how exactly
are we going to put this to rest?

10:47.980 --> 10:52.401
We have to take down the client
and make them withdraw the bounty.

10:52.485 --> 10:54.278
How reckless.

10:54.362 --> 10:56.656
The bounty's managed by the JAA.

10:56.739 --> 10:59.116
You won't figure out who put out the hit.

10:59.200 --> 11:02.912
I suppose our boss
probably has some contacts in the JAA.

11:02.995 --> 11:06.332
Well then, why don't you ask
your boss from Dondenkai for us?

11:06.415 --> 11:08.417
Why would I do that for you?

11:09.085 --> 11:11.128
I don't know where my boss is, anyway.

11:11.212 --> 11:12.755
What? You're useless.

11:12.838 --> 11:15.007
You're the one asking too much of people!

11:17.551 --> 11:19.095
Anyway… We'll be going now.

11:19.178 --> 11:21.138
See ya, Sakamoto.

11:21.222 --> 11:23.766
Bye guys, send my love to Lu.

11:26.727 --> 11:28.270
Now what?

11:28.354 --> 11:31.774
We still don't know where
the Dondenkai headquarters is.

11:32.691 --> 11:34.276
I might know someone.

11:39.698 --> 11:41.200
What's wrong with you?

11:41.283 --> 11:42.827
Got a tummy ache?

11:42.910 --> 11:46.455
Mr. Sakamoto
regained all his weight in a day.

11:46.539 --> 11:49.708
Oh, yeah.
I'm not surprised, seeing how he eats.

11:57.341 --> 11:58.467
This is it.

11:58.551 --> 11:59.385
Huh?

11:59.468 --> 12:01.929
VIDEO RENTALS

12:08.519 --> 12:09.520
ORDER VIDEOS NOT IN STOCK

12:09.603 --> 12:10.438
Let's see…

12:10.521 --> 12:13.107
A, B, C, D…

12:13.190 --> 12:14.191
Here it is.

12:16.610 --> 12:18.946
Yikes. Looks like a B-movie.

12:19.029 --> 12:22.741
Mr. Sakamoto. What is this place, anyway?

12:22.825 --> 12:23.951
They sell information.

12:24.535 --> 12:27.246
All information is sold in movie form.

12:27.329 --> 12:29.623
Why bother making them into movies?

12:29.707 --> 12:32.042
Come, the screening room's over here.

12:35.796 --> 12:39.133
<i>Dondenkai is a hit man organization</i>
<i>with over 50 members.</i>

12:39.925 --> 12:43.179
<i>Their story begins with one hit man.</i>

12:43.721 --> 12:45.514
<i>That's a nice building.</i>

12:45.598 --> 12:47.600
<i>Let's make this our headquarters.</i>

12:47.683 --> 12:49.894
<i>-Agreed!</i>
-So that's their headquarters.

12:50.686 --> 12:52.313
<i>Don't you die on me!</i>

12:52.897 --> 12:56.942
<i>Keep it down, you… dumbass…</i>

12:59.737 --> 13:02.072
That was such a good movie!

13:02.156 --> 13:05.451
Man, what a plot twist.
I thought they were done in that den…

13:05.534 --> 13:07.578
Director Kanaguri did it again.

13:08.787 --> 13:11.790
That'll be 756,000 yen.

13:11.874 --> 13:12.875
-So pricey!
-So pricey!

13:12.958 --> 13:14.043
I'll pay by card.

13:14.126 --> 13:15.085
Sure.

13:15.169 --> 13:17.338
You have that kind of money?

13:17.880 --> 13:20.090
I have savings from my bachelor days.

13:22.218 --> 13:25.304
Are you coming back to our world,
Mr. Sakamoto?

13:27.014 --> 13:29.391
I suggest you be cautious.

13:29.975 --> 13:32.561
Someone you used to work with
might be involved.

13:33.437 --> 13:34.522
What do you mean?

13:35.064 --> 13:38.192
I'm afraid that movie's not available yet.

13:38.734 --> 13:41.445
I've told you everything I can.

13:43.405 --> 13:47.034
Yo, I heard you met with Sakamoto.
That true, Nagumo?

13:47.117 --> 13:49.328
What? Sakamoto?

13:49.411 --> 13:52.456
What a blast from the past.
I wonder how he's doing?

13:52.540 --> 13:54.500
Don't play dumb with me.

13:55.292 --> 13:56.627
I'll kill you.

13:56.710 --> 14:00.005
Hyo, don't get into that now.

14:00.464 --> 14:02.258
The gent will be here any minute.

14:02.341 --> 14:04.176
I don't care.

14:04.260 --> 14:07.263
There's something shady about Nagumo!

14:07.763 --> 14:09.098
That's dangerous.

14:09.181 --> 14:12.184
Why don't we save the big knife
for the entrée, okay?

14:13.852 --> 14:17.815
My, my, so testy.
Not our cup of tea, is it, Osaragi?

14:18.274 --> 14:19.483
Mr. Shishiba,

14:19.984 --> 14:22.862
I don't think you want to eat that.

14:23.821 --> 14:25.155
Chef?

14:25.239 --> 14:26.574
Yes, sir?

14:29.702 --> 14:34.123
What are these blasted onions
doing in my risotto?

14:35.624 --> 14:41.422
Greetings, everyone.
Thank you very much for coming today.

14:42.506 --> 14:46.510
I am Iriya from the JAA.

14:47.094 --> 14:48.512
I must say,

14:48.596 --> 14:52.808
having all members of The Order together
is quite an extraordinary sight.

14:52.892 --> 14:57.313
You mean <i>some</i> members.
Where are the other four?

14:57.396 --> 15:00.858
Well, <i>those</i> three never come,

15:00.941 --> 15:03.736
but Takamura's not here?
That geezer always comes.

15:03.819 --> 15:05.821
Maybe he's busy?

15:05.905 --> 15:08.782
Doubt it. I bet he's forgotten.

15:08.866 --> 15:10.367
He's practically a fossil.

15:10.451 --> 15:14.288
Recently, someone has been going around

15:14.371 --> 15:18.626
butchering hit men in the JAA,
one after another.

15:18.709 --> 15:24.256
The JAA wishes to request your services
to take care of the matter immediately,

15:24.965 --> 15:27.217
<i>in the name of The Order.</i>

15:28.469 --> 15:30.638
This is Dondenkai HQ.

15:30.721 --> 15:33.182
Let's avoid combat as much as possible.

15:35.935 --> 15:37.728
Time for a stealth mission.

15:39.229 --> 15:41.732
Hey, did you hear about Sakamoto?

15:41.815 --> 15:44.360
Yeah. Crazy bounty, right?

15:44.443 --> 15:46.612
I heard that he got Boiled.

15:46.695 --> 15:50.240
Seriously? Not even Boiled could do it?

15:53.285 --> 15:55.371
I won't be pushing my luck.

16:03.087 --> 16:05.005
We're in.

16:05.089 --> 16:06.757
You're taking it off?

16:06.840 --> 16:07.967
Got bored of it.

16:08.050 --> 16:09.677
Where is this "boss" anyway?

16:10.302 --> 16:13.514
Were you not paying attention
to that expensive movie?

16:14.598 --> 16:16.642
The boss's room is on the top floor.

16:16.725 --> 16:19.061
We have to climb up
from the second-floor window.

16:19.144 --> 16:20.729
Like in the movie, remember?

16:20.813 --> 16:22.690
Right, Mr. Sakamoto?

16:22.773 --> 16:24.066
<i>I fell asleep.</i>

16:48.590 --> 16:51.301
This is fun. It's kinda like we're spies.

16:51.385 --> 16:53.137
You idiot, we're not here to play.

16:53.220 --> 16:54.096
HAVING A BLAST

16:58.517 --> 16:59.852
Something's off, Mr. Sakamoto.

16:59.935 --> 17:02.855
I can't hear any enemies on this floor.

17:03.939 --> 17:05.607
<i>What a useless detector.</i>

17:05.691 --> 17:08.110
I can hear <i>you,</i> you know!

17:10.320 --> 17:11.155
This is it.

17:29.006 --> 17:30.758
Hi, Sakamoto.

17:31.550 --> 17:32.468
Nagumo?

17:33.552 --> 17:35.637
You caught me red-handed.

17:35.721 --> 17:37.014
What are you doing here?

17:37.598 --> 17:41.477
Everyone in Dondenkai's upper management,
including the boss…

17:42.811 --> 17:44.605
has been killed by me.

17:45.773 --> 17:50.527
Sorry Sakamoto, but you have to die too.

17:58.118 --> 17:58.952
<i>He's so fast!</i>

18:01.455 --> 18:02.664
Shin!

18:11.090 --> 18:13.675
Just kidding! You should see your faces.

18:14.384 --> 18:15.594
I'm sorry, guys.

18:15.677 --> 18:17.638
I had an errand of my own.

18:17.721 --> 18:20.557
By the time I got here,
they had all been wiped out.

18:20.641 --> 18:22.351
Why didn't you just say so?!

18:22.434 --> 18:24.311
You're such a jerk!

18:24.394 --> 18:25.354
Why are you here?

18:25.979 --> 18:27.689
I guess I'd call it research.

18:28.315 --> 18:31.735
There have been
a lot of hits on hit men recently.

18:31.819 --> 18:34.696
What's so special about that?

18:34.780 --> 18:38.200
Sure, if it were just little quarrels
between hit men,

18:38.283 --> 18:40.202
no one would bat an eye.

18:40.828 --> 18:45.040
But over 100 hit men from organizations
close to the JAA

18:45.124 --> 18:47.960
have been murdered cruelly
in the last few months.

18:48.043 --> 18:50.671
It's obvious they're sending a message
to the JAA.

18:50.754 --> 18:52.881
One hundred hit men?

18:52.965 --> 18:55.300
But that's a quarter
of all professional hit men.

18:55.384 --> 18:58.846
They always leave an X at the scene,

18:58.929 --> 19:01.473
so we've been calling them "X" or "Slur."

19:01.557 --> 19:02.933
We?

19:03.016 --> 19:04.560
The Order has been assigned?

19:04.643 --> 19:05.477
Yep.

19:05.561 --> 19:08.814
The guy with the silver hair
was talking about that too.

19:08.897 --> 19:10.149
What is "The Order"?

19:10.232 --> 19:12.818
A special task unit for the JAA.

19:13.735 --> 19:15.946
<i>The best of the best among hit men.</i>

19:16.446 --> 19:21.160
<i>We report directly to the JAA and take on</i>
<i>hits on particularly dangerous hit men.</i>

19:21.243 --> 19:23.996
<i>We maintain order in the world of hit men.</i>

19:24.079 --> 19:27.082
Sakamoto used to be in The Order, too.

19:29.585 --> 19:31.128
<i>I had no idea.</i>

19:31.670 --> 19:33.088
Anyway, Sakamoto,

19:33.630 --> 19:36.133
you should all be careful of X.

19:36.216 --> 19:38.510
We're not hit men anymore.

19:38.594 --> 19:40.345
They don't have anything to do with us.

19:40.429 --> 19:41.513
That's right.

19:41.597 --> 19:44.057
We've already got our hands full
with the stupid bounty.

19:44.766 --> 19:47.394
I don't know much either, but…

19:47.477 --> 19:49.229
there is one thing I can tell you.

19:49.980 --> 19:52.482
These hits on hit men started

19:52.566 --> 19:58.113
right around the time
Sakamoto's bounty was posted.

20:01.950 --> 20:02.784
LEARN TO DRAW

20:02.868 --> 20:04.369
"When looking with both eyes,

20:04.953 --> 20:08.665
humans unconsciously correct
what they're seeing based on the angle."

20:09.625 --> 20:12.920
"Always take a step back to check

20:13.003 --> 20:14.796
that your drawing is symmetrical."

20:16.548 --> 20:17.382
Indeed.

20:17.883 --> 20:20.135
It may be slightly off-balance.

20:21.178 --> 20:22.012
SAKAMOTO'S

20:22.095 --> 20:23.388
We did all that,

20:23.472 --> 20:25.641
and we're back to square one.

20:26.391 --> 20:27.643
Listen up!

20:27.726 --> 20:29.811
-Where's Sakamoto?
-Another one?

20:29.895 --> 20:31.480
-I'll kill him!
-Getting a lot today.

20:31.563 --> 20:32.731
This one?

20:32.814 --> 20:35.734
No, the one right next to it.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.528
Sakamoto--

20:39.363 --> 20:42.741
We can't keep having
all these hit men dropping in.

20:42.824 --> 20:45.994
Who knew it'd be so hard
to get a bounty called off…

20:46.078 --> 20:47.162
Then again,

20:47.246 --> 20:50.290
bandage and band-aid sales are up,
so I guess it's okay.

20:51.041 --> 20:52.334
<i>That makes it okay?</i>

20:52.417 --> 20:54.461
Here, I have a band-aid for you.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.338
Thank you, little girl…

20:56.421 --> 20:58.048
Your daddy's so strong.

20:58.674 --> 20:59.591
<i>Sakamoto,</i>

21:00.384 --> 21:02.552
if you were neck and neck with Boiled,

21:02.636 --> 21:04.721
you're in for a world of hurt.

21:04.805 --> 21:07.975
It seems those five years
made a bigger dent than you thought.

21:09.059 --> 21:13.188
Since we don't know who the enemy is,
all we can do right now

21:13.272 --> 21:16.149
is become stronger
so we're prepared for any attack.

21:16.900 --> 21:18.443
Right. Make a full recovery.

21:22.572 --> 21:23.782
So fast!

21:24.950 --> 21:25.784
Welcome!

21:29.496 --> 21:30.622
Your items, miss!

21:30.706 --> 21:32.165
What? Ew!

21:33.166 --> 21:34.584
For my training,

21:34.668 --> 21:36.420
I'll drink myself stupid!

21:40.299 --> 21:41.174
Pork bun, please.

21:41.258 --> 21:42.342
Comin' right up!

21:42.426 --> 21:43.635
Lu!

21:43.719 --> 21:45.929
<i>How… did she know?</i>

21:46.013 --> 21:50.142
Hey, mister? Looks like you've got blood
gushing out of your forehead.

21:50.976 --> 21:52.936
Shin, what do we do?

21:53.020 --> 21:54.813
He's thinking bandage. Here!

21:54.896 --> 21:55.939
Shin…

23:20.941 --> 23:25.946
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
